#!/bin/sh
# Installs dsh-gitlab-superagent into a DSH profile in one step: creates the profile from the
# shipped web template when needed, installs the bundle from the repository, and writes the
# stateDir/port overrides. Does not need a checkout of this repository to run.
set -eu

repo='Santinell/dsh-gitlab-superagent'
profile=${DSH_PROFILE:-superagent}
port=${DSH_PORT:-3082}
ref=${DSH_REF:-main}
state_dir=${DSH_STATE_DIR:-}
dsh_cmd=${DSH_CMD:-'bunx @deepseek-ai/dsh@next'}
recreate='0'
force_patch='0'
dry_run='0'

truthy() { case "$1" in ''|0|false|no|off) return 1 ;; *) return 0 ;; esac; }
if truthy "${DSH_RECREATE:-0}"; then recreate='1'; fi
if truthy "${DSH_FORCE_PATCH:-0}"; then force_patch='1'; fi
if truthy "${DSH_DRY_RUN:-0}"; then dry_run='1'; fi

usage() {
  cat <<'TXT'
Usage: install-dsh [options]

Options:
  --profile NAME    DSH profile to install into (default: superagent)
  --port PORT       Web UI port written to the profile overrides (default: 3082)
  --state-dir PATH  New absolute stateDir (default: <DSH_HOME>/state/<profile>-gitlab)
  --ref REF         Git ref of the plugin repository (default: main)
  --dsh CMD         DSH command (default: bunx @deepseek-ai/dsh@next)
  --recreate        Replace an existing profile from the web template (discards its config and patch)
  --force-patch     Overwrite cordis.patch.yml even when it already has custom entries
  --dry-run         Print the planned commands without running them
  -h, --help        Show this help

Environment (a flag wins over its variable):
  DSH_PROFILE DSH_PORT DSH_STATE_DIR DSH_REF DSH_CMD
  DSH_RECREATE DSH_FORCE_PATCH DSH_DRY_RUN   (1, true, yes or on enables)
  DSH_HOME                                   (profile root, default: ~/.dsh)

The script needs DSH and pnpm. It writes <DSH_HOME>/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml,
so an existing patch is left untouched unless --force-patch is given.
TXT
}

while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --profile) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo 'install-dsh: --profile needs a value' >&2; exit 1; }; profile=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --port) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo 'install-dsh: --port needs a value' >&2; exit 1; }; port=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --state-dir) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo 'install-dsh: --state-dir needs a value' >&2; exit 1; }; state_dir=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --ref) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo 'install-dsh: --ref needs a value' >&2; exit 1; }; ref=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --dsh) [ "$#" -ge 2 ] || { echo 'install-dsh: --dsh needs a value' >&2; exit 1; }; dsh_cmd=$2; shift 2 ;;
    --recreate) recreate='1'; shift ;;
    --force-patch) force_patch='1'; shift ;;
    --dry-run) dry_run='1'; shift ;;
    -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
    *) echo "install-dsh: unknown option: $1" >&2; usage >&2; exit 1 ;;
  esac
done

say() { printf '%s\n' "$*"; }
warn() { printf 'install-dsh: %s\n' "$*" >&2; }
die() { warn "$*"; exit 1; }

case "$port" in
  ''|*[!0-9]*) die "--port must be a number" ;;
esac

if [ -z "$dsh_cmd" ]; then
  die "--dsh/DSH_CMD must not be empty"
fi

command -v pnpm >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "pnpm is not on PATH; 'dsh plugin' forwards to pnpm"

dsh_home=${DSH_HOME:-"$HOME/.dsh"}
[ -n "$state_dir" ] || state_dir="$dsh_home/state/$profile-gitlab"
case "$state_dir" in
  /*) ;;
  *) die "--state-dir must be an absolute path" ;;
esac
profile_dir="$dsh_home/profiles/$profile"
patch_file="$profile_dir/cordis.patch.yml"

# The DSH command may be a single word or a fixed prefix such as "bunx @deepseek-ai/dsh@next".
run_dsh() { $dsh_cmd "$@"; }
run_plan() {
  if [ "$dry_run" = '1' ]; then say "+ $*"; else "$@"; fi
}

say "DSH_HOME: $dsh_home"
say "Profile:  $profile"
say "Plugin:   $repo#$ref"
say "stateDir: $state_dir"
say "Port:     $port"
say ''

if [ -d "$profile_dir" ]; then
  if [ "$recreate" = '1' ]; then
    say "Replacing profile '$profile' from the web template..."
    run_plan $dsh_cmd "$profile" --from-default-profile web --dump-config
  elif grep -q '"@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app"' "$profile_dir/package.json" 2>/dev/null; then
    say "Profile '$profile' already exists; keeping its configuration."
  else
    die "profile '$profile' exists without the web app bundle; rerun with --recreate (it replaces the profile) or choose another --profile"
  fi
else
  say "Creating profile '$profile' from the web template..."
  run_plan $dsh_cmd "$profile" --from-default-profile web --dump-config
fi

say "Installing the plugin..."
if [ "$dry_run" = '1' ]; then
  say "+ $dsh_cmd plugin --profile $profile add \"github:$repo#$ref\""
else
  run_dsh plugin --profile "$profile" add "github:$repo#$ref"
fi

if [ "$dry_run" != '1' ]; then
  say "Verifying the composed profile..."
  run_dsh --profile "$profile" --dump-config >/dev/null
fi

umask 077
previous_umask=$(umask)
run_plan mkdir -p "$state_dir"
umask "$previous_umask"

escaped_state=$(printf '%s' "$state_dir" | sed 's/\\/\\\\/g; s/"/\\"/g')
patch_body=$(printf -- '- id: webserver\n  config:\n    host: 127.0.0.1\n    port: %s\n- id: dsh-superagent\n  config:\n    stateDir: "%s"\n' "$port" "$escaped_state")
patch_marker='# Managed by scripts/install-dsh; rerun the installer to update, or remove this line to edit by hand.'

meaningful=''
managed='0'
if [ -f "$patch_file" ]; then
  meaningful=$(grep -v '^[[:space:]]*#' "$patch_file" 2>/dev/null | grep -v '^[[:space:]]*$' || true)
  if grep -q 'Managed by scripts/install-dsh' "$patch_file" 2>/dev/null; then managed='1'; fi
fi

write_patch() {
  if [ "$dry_run" = '1' ]; then
    say "Would write $patch_file:"
    printf '%s\n' "$patch_body"
  else
    {
      printf '%s\n' "$patch_marker"
      printf '# Keep the entry IDs stable; the profile and stateDir identify this installation.\n'
      printf '%s\n' "$patch_body"
    } > "$patch_file"
    say "Wrote $patch_file"
  fi
}

if [ "$dry_run" = '1' ]; then
  write_patch
elif [ -z "$meaningful" ] || [ "$meaningful" = '[]' ] || [ "$managed" = '1' ]; then
  write_patch
elif [ "$force_patch" = '1' ]; then
  say "Overwriting the existing profile patch (--force-patch)."
  write_patch
else
  warn "$patch_file already has custom entries; not overwriting it."
  warn "Add these entries yourself (or rerun with --force-patch):"
  printf '%s\n' "$patch_body" >&2
  exit 2
fi

say ''
say "Done. Start the profile with:"
say "  $dsh_cmd --profile $profile --no-open"
say "or omit --no-open to open the panel in a browser. The first start reports projectUnset"
say "until the GitLab Source (project, host, glab-agent CLI) is saved in the panel."
